When maintaining/updating the annotations, follow the following steps.

1. Generate a kernel tree, easiest way as follows ...

     ciel sh
     acbs-build linux-kernel	(wait for it to fail, or ^C after all patches
				 are applied)

2. Re-generate an unmodified .config ...

     annotations -a $ARCH -l main -e -f autobuild/annotations.mainline

     ... or annotations.retro when maintaining Afterglow architectures.

3. Work through all new/changed options ...

     make oldconfig		(this is interactive)

4. Write back the changes to the annotations ...

     annotations -a $ARCH -l main -u .config \
         -f /tree/runtime-kernel/linux-kernel/autobuild/annotations.mainline

     ... or annotations.retro, you get the idea.

5. Test your changes ...

     acbs-build linux-kernel

6. Repeat the process until the configuration check passes.

---

Extra notes for loongarch64:

1. When updating annotations, use `-l main' instead of `-l main-{4,16}k'.
2. Read the Git diff, and revise all page-related options back to the
   correspondent flavour (should be obvious).
